Package: worksuite-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: worksuite-shell, worksuite-session, worksuite-branding, worksuite-archive-keyring,
 worksuite-user-services, worksuite-ai, worksuite-package-service, worksuite-device-agent, worksuite-directory, worksuite-recovery-boot, worksuite-wayland-bridge,
 labwc, wlr-randr, greetd, cage, gtkgreet | worksuite-greeter, gtklock, swayidle,
 xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-desktop-portal-wlr, grim, wl-clipboard, wtype, xdg-desktop-portal-gtk, gnome-keyring,
 pipewire, pipewire-pulse, wireplumber, network-manager, wpasupplicant, rfkill, bluez, udisks2, upower, cups, cups-filters, avahi-daemon, libnss-mdns, polkitd, pkexec,
 flatpak, fcitx5, fcitx5-m17n, fcitx5-frontend-gtk3, fcitx5-frontend-gtk4, fcitx5-frontend-qt6, apparmor, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: cups-browsed, ipp-usb, cups-ipp-utils, printer-driver-gutenprint, fwupd, wl-mirror, iw, vainfo, vulkan-tools, mesa-va-drivers, libgl1-mesa-dri, worksuite-office | worksuite-desktopeditors
Conflicts: openssh-server
Description: WorkSuite OS desktop (metapackage)
 Pulls in the WorkSuite session, shell, system services and the Debian
 desktop stack they rely on. No SSH server (WSOS-SEC-010). The WorkSuite web
 apps (Mail, Calendar, Chat, Drive, ...) come with worksuite-shell; WorkSuite
 Office (native editors) is published separately and added to the image when
 its .deb is provided. The shell is also the panel (taskbar, tray,
 update badge); its window list comes from worksuite-wayland-bridge.

Package: worksuite-shell
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: libc6, libgtk-3-0t64 | libgtk-3-0, libgtk-3-bin, desktop-file-utils, libnss3, libasound2t64 | libasound2, libgbm1, libdrm2, libxshmfence1, wl-clipboard, grim, wtype, libsecret-tools, libwayland-client0, tar, gzip, xz-utils,
         7zip, libarchive-tools, fonts-noto-color-emoji, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: zip, unzip, bzip2, zstd
Description: WorkSuite shell (Electron launcher, dashboard, Settings, App Center)
 The React/Electron desktop shell of WorkSuite OS: greeter preview, launcher,
 desktop, Files, App Center, Settings, recovery launcher and installer UI,
 with a bundled Electron runtime. Also provides worksuite-node, the Node
 runtime the WorkSuite services run on, and worksuite-app, which opens each
 WorkSuite web app (Mail, Calendar, Chat, Drive, Tasks, Projects, CRM, Meet,
 PDF Studio) in its own window, with their menu entries, icons and the
 worksuite:// link handler.

Package: worksuite-wayland-bridge
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-pywayland, python3-cffi-backend, python3-dbus-next, labwc, grim, x11-utils, ${misc:Depends}
Description: WorkSuite Wayland bridge (window list, tray watcher) on D-Bus
 Session service lk.worksuite.WaylandBridge1: lists, activates, minimizes and
 closes Labwc windows through wlr-foreign-toplevel-management for the WorkSuite
 shell's panel only (caller verified by bus credentials). Also the
 StatusNotifierItem watcher and host behind the panel's tray.

Package: worksuite-session
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, labwc, xwayland, systemd, dbus-user-session, xdg-user-dirs, librsvg2-common, adwaita-icon-theme, gtklock, swayidle, wlopm, wlr-randr, wtype, python3-evdev, zenity, python3, pkexec | policykit-1, lxpolkit | mate-polkit, python3-gi, gir1.2-polkit-1.0,
 libpam-modules, libpam-runtime, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: python3, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-gtk4layershell-1.0, libgtk4-layer-shell0, wvkbd, libpam-u2f, pamu2fcfg
Description: WorkSuite Wayland session file, systemd user units and launcher
 Session entry for the display manager, the worksuite-session launcher and the
 systemd user units bound to worksuite-session.target, plus Labwc and portal
 configuration, the gtklock/swayidle screen lock, the polkit authentication
 agent, the greeter wrapper, the pam_faillock sign-in lockout and the device PIN
 and FIDO2 security-key sign-in (off until someone sets one up).

Package: worksuite-user-services
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: worksuite-shell (= ${binary:Version}), gnome-keyring, libpam-gnome-keyring, libsecret-tools, xdg-utils, ${misc:Depends}
Description: WorkSuite user services (catalog, files, credentials broker, sync)
 Per-user services: the offline-first sync service (local SQLite store and
 outbox) and the credentials broker (OneAuth sign-in, keyring-held refresh
 tokens).

Package: worksuite-ai
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: worksuite-shell (= ${binary:Version}), systemd, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: libvulkan1, mesa-vulkan-drivers
Description: WorkSuite AI assistant: models that run on this device
 Per-user service behind a 0600 Unix socket that runs a downloaded GGUF model
 with llama.cpp (node-llama-cpp, prebuilt CPU and Vulkan builds) for the
 shell's assistant. Inference runs in its own unit with no network and with
 memory and CPU limits. Models are never shipped in the image: they are
 downloaded over HTTPS from the packaged catalog's host, verified against a
 pinned SHA-256 before every load, and can be switched off or limited by the
 organization's device policy. Prompts and answers are never logged.

Package: worksuite-package-service
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: worksuite-shell (= ${binary:Version}), worksuite-archive-keyring, apt, flatpak, polkitd, dbus, gpg, squashfs-tools, ${misc:Depends}
Description: WorkSuite system package service (D-Bus + polkit)
 Root service on the system bus that installs, removes and updates APT and
 Flatpak software for the shell and the device agent, behind polkit, one job
 at a time.

Package: worksuite-device-agent
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: worksuite-shell (= ${binary:Version}), worksuite-archive-keyring, cryptsetup, dbus, systemd, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: tpm2-tools, network-manager, wireguard-tools, nftables, network-manager-openvpn, clamav, clamav-freshclam, clamav-daemon, clamdscan, dnsmasq-base
Description: WorkSuite device agent (enrollment, policy, signed remote commands)
 Root agent for organization-managed devices: enrollment, signed policy,
 heartbeat, signed remote commands and remote wipe.

Package: worksuite-directory
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: worksuite-shell (= ${binary:Version}), libpam-runtime, libpam-modules, passwd, bsdutils, systemd, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: worksuite-device-agent
Description: WorkSuite directory sign-in and break-glass admin
 Signs organization users in at the greeter through pam_exec and the
 WorkSuite directory endpoint, with a policy-limited offline cache, stable
 UIDs and role-to-group mapping, plus a locally escrowed, one-time-use
 break-glass administrator.

Package: worksuite-recovery-boot
Architecture: all
Depends: worksuite-shell, worksuite-session, cage, grub-common, dpkg, apt, systemd, passwd, squashfs-tools, util-linux, pkexec, ${misc:Depends}
Description: WorkSuite Recovery boot entry, previous-kernel retention and boot-time repair
 Adds the "WorkSuite Recovery" and "previous kernel" GRUB entries, keeps the
 previous kernel from apt autoremove, boots worksuite-recovery.target into
 the shell recovery screens, and repairs interrupted package operations
 before the greeter starts. Also reinstalls the system from the recovery
 image keeping /home (worksuite-reinstall).

Package: calamares-settings-worksuite
